{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b49591f5aa4f3ffa","type":"tool_result","content":"total 16\ndrwx------@  12 avalappi  staff    384 24 Oct 06:59 .\ndrwx------@ 474 avalappi  staff  15168 24 Oct 08:38 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@  12 avalappi  staff    384 24 Oct 06:59 .claude-config\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 avalappi  staff     96 23 Sep 12:54 .claude-plugin\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 avalappi  staff    128 23 Sep 12:54 .context\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 avalappi  staff     96 24 Oct 06:25 artifacts\n-rw-r--r--@   1 avalappi  staff   7393 24 Oct 06:25 CLAUDE.md\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 avalappi  staff     96 23 Sep 12:54 docs\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 avalappi  staff     96 23 Sep 12:54 hooks\ndrwxr-xr-x@  21 avalappi  staff    672 24 Oct 07:02 scripts\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 avalappi  staff     96 24 Oct 06:25 skills\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 avalappi  staff    224 24 Oct 07:02 tmp\n# Platform: RHOAI 3.6-ea.1\n\n## Metadata\n\n- **Distribution**: RHOAI\n- **Version**: 3.6-ea.1\n- **Base Platform**: OpenShift Container Platform v4.x\n- **Supported OCP Versions**: v4.16+\n- **Supported CPU Architectures**: amd64\n- **Total Shipped Container Images**: 72+\n- **Components Analyzed**: 72\n- **Generated By**: Claude Opus 4.6 on 2026-08-13\n\n## Platform Overview\n\nRed Hat OpenShift AI (RHOAI) 3.6-ea.1 is a comprehensive AI/ML platform deployed on OpenShift Container Platform through the Operator Lifecycle Manager (OLM). The platform is orchestrated by rhods-operator, which manages the lifecycle of all platform components through a hierarchy of custom resources — DataScienceCluster, DSCInitialization, and per-component CRDs. Each major capability (model serving, pipelines, distributed workloads, notebooks, model registry, training, observability, guardrails, and models-as-a-service) is implemented by a dedicated module operator or controller that watches its component CR and reconciles downstream Kubernetes resources using kustomize-based manifest rendering through the shared odh-platform-utilities framework.\n\nThe platform ingress architecture is in active transition. The rhods-operator Gateway service controller provisions a central `data-science-gateway` using Gateway API (GatewayClass, Gateway, HTTPRoutes) while maintaining backward compatibility through OpenShift Routes. kube-auth-proxy provides OIDC-authenticated access to the dashboard, and the Gateway controller conditionally integrates with Istio by dynamically creating EnvoyFilter and DestinationRule resources when Istio CRDs are detected. Models-as-a-Service introduces a parallel ingress path through Kuadrant AuthPolicy enforcement with API key, TokenReview, and optional OIDC JWT authentication at the Gateway level. Model-registry-operator implements dual ingress (Gateway API HTTPRoutes and OpenShift Routes) with kube-rbac-proxy sidecar authentication on backend pods.\n\nSecurity follows a defense-in-depth posture: all shipped Go binaries are built with `CGO_ENABLED=1` and `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime` for FIPS-compliant cryptography through system OpenSSL, operators read the cluster APIServer TLS security profile to align their TLS configuration with platform-wide policy, admission webhooks validate and default CRD resources with fail-closed policies, and per-component RBAC is scoped through dedicated ServiceAccounts and ClusterRoles. Authentication is layered across gateway-level (kube-auth-proxy OIDC, Kuadrant AuthPolicy), pod-level (kube-rbac-proxy sidecar), and application-level (Kubernetes TokenReview, SubjectAccessReview) enforcement points.\n\n## Component Relationships\n\n### Dependency Graph\n\n```\nrhods-operator\n|-- kserve (runtime-integration)\n|   `-- kube-rbac-proxy (unknown)\n|-- model-registry (unknown)\n|   `-- kserve (runtime-integration) (*)\n`-- models-as-a-service (runtime-library)\n    `-- kserve (runtime-integration) (*)\n\nLeaf components (no internal deps to/from other components):\n  MLServer\n  NeMo-Guardrails\n  argo-workflows\n  eval-hub\n  fms-guardrails-orchestrator\n  guardrails-regex-detector\n  kube-auth-proxy\n  llm-d-planner\n  lm-evaluation-harness\n  mcp-lifecycle-module-operator\n  mcp-lifecycle-operator\n  ml-metadata\n  model-metadata-collection\n  odh-cli\n  odh-observability\n  ogx-k8s-operator\n  OpenShell\n  rhaii-cluster-validation\n  spark-operator\n  trainer\n  trainer-operator\n  training_hub\n  training-operator\n  vllm-cpu\n  workload-variant-autoscaler","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9e151db733b34577","agent_id":"a2acd6dbbe0ab6692","session_id":"eeda53a7-63f0-4339-b053-cfdf4fd1df6d","uuid":"d8f5e1a3-0218-48fa-85f9-aeed18a57a67","timestamp":"2026-10-24T10:06:12.103Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b49591f5aa4f3ffa","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8010"}
